# Cursor Rules for Document Extraction API

## Code Style & Guidelines

- Language: Python 3.11+
- Framework: FastAPI with strict Pydantic v2 validation models.
- Always use type annotations (typing module or standard Python 3.10+ union types).
- Use async/await for all I/O-bound FastAPI endpoints and Supabase async client operations.
- Worker: Use Celery with Redis broker/backend or ARQ. Keep worker tasks modular under app/workers/.

## Gemini API Instructions

- Use the official google-genai SDK.
- For structured extraction, use Gemini's native structured outputs (response_mime_type="application/json" and pass response_schema or inject schema constraints into the prompt).
- Pass PDF directly as MIME application/pdf to the multimodal endpoint without needing local OCR / Tesseract.

## Error Handling & Security

- Never expose internal stack traces to the API client; return structured HTTP 4xx/5xx errors.
- Never store raw API keys; store hashes (hashlib.sha256) and look up by key prefix + hash verification.
- Always validate JSON schemas passed by users using jsonschema before passing to Gemini.
- Use environment variables via pydantic-settings (app/core/config.py).
